{"kind":"request","text":"NF-2: finish the MCP boundary. Move the bounded tool description to\npackages/mcp, and tie the act output schema to one typed result. One\nhead with checker review and the gate.\n\nThis is the work of planner request 0916128e. Hugh asked for it on 11\nNovember and said as soon as possible. Read 0916128e for the six\nproblems at main df41e599, the three parts and the size estimate. The\nhead follows NF-1 6050f6ea in the same lane.\n\nScope, as 0916128e states it.\n1. Move `DESCRIPTION_CHARS`, `Described` and `describeAct` to\n   packages/mcp. Delete the re-exports in packages/mcp/src/describe.ts\n   and at shape.ts:159. Each importer takes a name from its owner.\n2. One typed result in packages/mcp for an act, a step and an install,\n   built by one function from an `Answer`. `ACT_OUTPUT` lists every\n   member, and a `satisfies` clause fails the build when the two\n   differ. The in-process callers read the typed result, not\n   `structuredContent`.\n3. Audit each fixed tool: its hand-written input schema against its\n   parser. Report the table. Fix only a schema that admits a value\n   that the parser refuses, and list every other difference for me.\n\nRulings.\n- `effects`. The one result type carries the count of effects as an\n  optional member. The one function sets it whenever the answer took\n  effect, for an act, a step and an install alike.\n- `phase`. It stays a top-level member of the act result. Its\n  description says that it is where this client's kept request stands,\n  and that `answer` is the room's decision. Its values are the eight\n  custody words: `prepared`, `sent`, `unknown`, `accepted`, `archived`,\n  `refused`, `mismatch` and `settled`. The custody requests keep those\n  words.\n- The description of `answer` names every value, `archived` included.\n- Tool list bytes. Report the change against the MCP budget. Keep the\n  schema inline. If the change passes the budget, stop and tell me the\n  figures before you try `